EXPECTED: NO_DOS_EFFECT

REASON: quic-go enforces an internal send-buffer cap regardless of peer-advertised window

TARGET_IMAGE: caddy:2.8.4
TARGET_PORT: 443/udp
CLIENT_TOOL: aioquic

DISPROOF_METHOD: assumption_refuted
DISPROOF_DETAIL: |
  Opened 100 QUIC connections, each advertising a 1 GB initial receive window
  then immediately stalling (zero recv() calls). quic-go capped per-connection
  send buffer at ~10 MB and began dropping blocked streams after the buffer-full
  timeout. Server memory stayed within 50 MB above baseline. CPU stayed below 8%.
  No observable resource accumulation; connections were eventually torn down cleanly.
DISPROOF_NOTES: Assumption A1 ("no internal cap") is refuted. quic-go's flowcontrol
                package applies a WriterToBeFlowControlBlocked cap independent of
                the peer-advertised window.
